{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj | sed -n '1,440p'; nl -ba test/yang/php/antlr/programs_p5.cljc; rg -n 'normal|headers|errno|p5' test/yang/php/antlr/request_context_test*; cat collab/orch-lane/*p5*findings*\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yang.php.oracle\n     2\t  \"PHP 8.3 CLI oracle runner for `yang.php.antlr.programs`\n     3\t   (docs/design/yang.php.md sections 14, 17.3).\n     4\t\n     5\t   For every fixture in `programs/fixtures` (plus `matrix-source` and\n     6\t   `float-cases`), writes the PHP source to a temporary file and runs:\n     7\t     docker run --rm -v <dir>:/w -w /w php:8.3-cli php \\\\\n     8\t       -d display_errors=1 -d html_errors=0 -d error_reporting=E_ALL \\\\\n     9\t       -d log_errors=0 <file>\n    10\t   Parses stdout into `:out`, `:diag` (`[[errno message] ...]`) and `:uncaught`\n    11\t   (`{:class c :message m}`), and compares against each fixture's expectation\n    12\t   (or `:departure/:zend` for departure fixtures).\"\n    13\t  (:require\n    14\t    [clojure.java.io :as io]\n    15\t    [clojure.java.shell :as sh]\n    16\t    [clojure.string :as str]\n    17\t    [yang.php.antlr.programs :as programs]\n    18\t    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p3b :as p3b]\n    19\t    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p4 :as p4]\n    20\t    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p5 :as p5]\n    21\t    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p6 :as p6])\n    22\t  (:import\n    23\t    (java.nio.charset\n    24\t      StandardCharsets)\n    25\t    (java.nio.file\n    26\t      Files)\n    27\t    (java.nio.file.attribute\n    28\t      FileAttribute)))\n    29\t\n    30\t\n    31\t(def banner\n    32\t  \"The pinned PHP 8.3 CLI oracle provenance banner.\"\n    33\t  p3b/banner)\n    34\t\n    35\t\n    36\t(def ^:private errno-of\n    37\t  {\"Warning\" 2,\n    38\t   \"Notice\" 8,\n    39\t   \"Deprecated\" 8192,\n    40\t   \"Fatal error\" 1})\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\t(defn- location-pattern\n    44\t  \"The regex source of a PHP source location below `/w/`: the entry `file`\n    45\t   itself, or, for a multi-unit fixture run in `/w/<unit-dir>`, any unit file\n    46\t   below the directory.\"\n    47\t  [file unit-dir]\n    48\t  (if unit-dir\n    49\t    (str (java.util.regex.Pattern/quote unit-dir) \"/[^\\\\s:]+\")\n    50\t    (java.util.regex.Pattern/quote file)))\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\t(defn- strip-location\n    54\t  ([s file] (strip-location s file nil))\n    55\t  ([s file unit-dir]\n    56\t   (str/replace s\n    57\t                (re-pattern (str \" in /w/\" (location-pattern file unit-dir) \" on line \\\\d+\"))\n    58\t                \"\")))\n    59\t\n    60\t\n    61\t(defn parse-stdout\n    62\t  \"Parse PHP CLI stdout for `/w/<file>` into\n    63\t   `{:out <string> :diag [[errno msg] ...] :uncaught {:class c :message m}-or-nil}`.\n    64\t   With `unit-dir`, locations in any file below `/w/<unit-dir>` are stripped\n    65\t   (a multi-unit fixture).\"\n    66\t  ([raw file] (parse-stdout raw file nil))\n    67\t  ([raw file unit-dir]\n    68\t   (let [qfile (location-pattern file unit-dir)\n    69\t         strip-location (fn [s file] (strip-location s file unit-dir))\n    70\t         ;; The uncaught block ends at PHP's own terminator, so output written\n    71\t         ;; after it (shutdown functions, destructors) stays in :out.\n    72\t         uncaught-re (re-pattern\n    73\t                       (str \"(?s)\\\\nFatal error: Uncaught ([^:]+): ([^\\\\r\\\\n]*) in /w/\"\n    74\t                            qfile\n    75\t                            \":\\\\d+\\\\nStack trace:\\\\n.*?\\\\n  thrown in /w/\"\n    76\t                            qfile\n    77\t                            \" on line \\\\d+\\\\n\"))\n    78\t         fatal-re (re-pattern\n    79\t                    (str \"\\\\nFatal error: ([^\\\\r\\\\n]*) in /w/\"\n    80\t                         qfile\n    81\t                         \" on line \\\\d+\\\\n\"))\n    82\t         diag-re (re-pattern\n    83\t                   (str \"\\\\n(Warning|Notice|Deprecated): ([^\\\\r\\\\n]*?) in /w/\"\n    84\t                        qfile\n    85\t                        \" on line \\\\d+\\\\n\"))\n    86\t         [without-fatal uncaught]\n    87\t         (if-let [[_ cls msg] (re-find uncaught-re raw)]\n    88\t           [(str/replace raw uncaught-re \"\")\n    89\t            {:class cls, :message (strip-location msg file)}]\n    90\t           (if-let [[_ msg] (re-find fatal-re raw)]\n    91\t             [(str/replace raw fatal-re \"\")\n    92\t              {:class \"Error\", :message (strip-location msg file)}]\n    93\t             [raw nil]))\n    94\t         diags (volatile! [])\n    95\t         out (str/replace without-fatal\n    96\t                          diag-re\n    97\t                          (fn [[_ kind msg]]\n    98\t                            (vswap! diags conj [(get errno-of kind) (strip-location msg file)])\n    99\t                            \"\"))]\n   100\t     {:out out,\n   101\t      :diag @diags,\n   102\t      :uncaught uncaught})))\n   103\t\n   104\t\n   105\t(defn run-php-file\n   106\t  \"Run `<file>` inside `<dir>` via Docker `php:8.3-cli` and return the parsed\n   107\t   `{:out :diag :uncaught :exit}`. With `unit-dir`, the working directory is\n   108\t   `/w/<unit-dir>` and `file` is relative to it (a multi-unit fixture).\"\n   109\t  ([dir file] (run-php-file dir file nil))\n   110\t  ([dir file unit-dir]\n   111\t   (let [{:keys [out err exit]}\n   112\t         (sh/sh \"docker\" \"run\" \"--rm\"\n   113\t                \"-v\" (str (.toAbsolutePath (.toPath (io/file dir))) \":/w\")\n   114\t                \"-w\" (if unit-dir (str \"/w/\" unit-dir) \"/w\")\n   115\t                \"php:8.3-cli\" \"php\"\n   116\t                \"-d\" \"display_errors=1\"\n   117\t                \"-d\" \"html_errors=0\"\n   118\t                \"-d\" \"error_reporting=E_ALL\"\n   119\t                \"-d\" \"log_errors=0\"\n   120\t                file\n   121\t                :out-enc \"UTF-8\")]\n   122\t     (assoc (parse-stdout out (if unit-dir (str unit-dir \"/\" file) file) unit-dir)\n   123\t            :err err\n   124\t            :exit exit))))\n   125\t\n   126\t\n   127\t(defn- write-source!\n   128\t  [dir file ^String source]\n   129\t  (Files/write (.toPath (io/file dir file))\n   130\t               (.getBytes source StandardCharsets/UTF_8)\n   131\t               (make-array java.nio.file.OpenOption 0)))\n   132\t\n   133\t\n   134\t(defn- unit-actual\n   135\t  \"Run the multi-unit `fixture`: every unit is written below `<dir>/<id>/`,\n   136\t   `main.php` is run with that directory as the working directory, and\n   137\t   `/w/<id>` is replaced by `.` in everything the program printed (the\n   138\t   comparison's definition, plan P6 2.5 rule 2; corner C37).\"\n   139\t  [dir {:keys [id units main], :or {main \"main.php\"}}]\n   140\t  (let [unit-dir (name id)\n   141\t        norm (fn [s] (str/replace s (str \"/w/\" unit-dir) \".\"))]\n   142\t    (doseq [[path source] units]\n   143\t      (let [f (io/file dir unit-dir path)]\n   144\t        (io/make-parents f)\n   145\t        (write-source! dir (str unit-dir \"/\" path) source)))\n   146\t    (let [actual (run-php-file dir main unit-dir)]\n   147\t      (-> actual\n   148\t          (update :out norm)\n   149\t          (update :diag (fn [ds] (mapv (fn [[errno msg]] [errno (norm msg)]) ds)))\n   150\t          (update :uncaught #(some-> % (update :message norm)))))))\n   151\t\n   152\t\n   153\t(defn check-fixture\n   154\t  \"Run `fixture` in temporary directory `dir` and return a check record.\"\n   155\t  [dir {:keys [id source units out diag uncaught departure gap oracle], :as fixture}]\n   156\t  (let [file (str (name id) \".php\")]\n   157\t    (when-not units (write-source! dir file source))\n   158\t    (let [actual (if units (unit-actual dir fixture) (run-php-file dir file))\n   159\t          expected-out (cond departure (:zend departure)\n   160\t                             gap \"\"\n   161\t                             :else out)\n   162\t          expected-diag (vec (cond departure (:zend-diag departure)\n   163\t                                   gap []\n   164\t                                   :else (or diag [])))\n   165\t          expected-uncaught (cond departure (:zend-uncaught departure)\n   166\t                                  gap nil\n   167\t                                  :else uncaught)\n   168\t          pass? (and (not= :pending oracle)\n   169\t                     (= expected-out (:out actual))\n   170\t                     (= expected-diag (:diag actual))\n   171\t                     (= expected-uncaught (:uncaught actual)))]\n   172\t      {:id id,\n   173\t       :pass? pass?,\n   174\t       :oracle oracle,\n   175\t       :gap gap,\n   176\t       :departure departure,\n   177\t       :expected {:out expected-out, :diag expected-diag, :uncaught expected-uncaught},\n   178\t       :actual (select-keys actual [:out :diag :uncaught])})))\n   179\t\n   180\t\n   181\t(defn- check-matrix\n   182\t  [dir]\n   183\t  (let [file \"scalar-comparison-matrix.php\"\n   184\t        _ (write-source! dir file programs/matrix-source)\n   185\t        actual (run-php-file dir file)\n   186\t        [eq sp] (str/split-lines (:out actual))\n   187\t        w (count programs/matrix-values)\n   188\t        actual-eq (mapv #(apply str %) (partition w eq))\n   189\t        actual-sp (mapv #(apply str (map {\\0 \"<\", \\1 \"=\", \\2 \">\"} %)) (partition w sp))]\n   190\t    {:id :scalar-comparison-matrix,\n   191\t     :pass? (and (= programs/equal-matrix actual-eq)\n   192\t                 (= programs/spaceship-matrix actual-sp)\n   193\t                 (empty? (:diag actual))\n   194\t                 (nil? (:uncaught actual))),\n   195\t     :expected {:eq programs/equal-matrix, :sp programs/spaceship-matrix},\n   196\t     :actual {:eq actual-eq, :sp actual-sp, :diag (:diag actual), :uncaught (:uncaught actual)}}))\n   197\t\n   198\t\n   199\t(defn- check-floats\n   200\t  [dir]\n   201\t  (let [file \"float-cases.php\"\n   202\t        src (str \"<?php\\n\"\n   203\t                 (apply str (for [[lit] programs/float-cases]\n   204\t                              (str \"echo \" lit \", \\\"|\\\"; var_dump(\" lit \");\\n\"))))\n   205\t        expected (apply str (for [[_ echo dump] programs/float-cases]\n   206\t                              (str echo \"|float(\" dump \")\\n\")))\n   207\t        _ (write-source! dir file src)\n   208\t        actual (run-php-file dir file)]\n   209\t    {:id :float-cases,\n   210\t     :pass? (and (= expected (:out actual))\n   211\t                 (empty? (:diag actual))\n   212\t                 (nil? (:uncaught actual))),\n   213\t     :expected {:out expected, :diag [], :uncaught nil},\n   214\t     :actual (select-keys actual [:out :diag :uncaught])}))\n   215\t\n   216\t\n   217\t(defn- php-literal\n   218\t  \"The PHP literal of request-record scalar `v`: strings single-quoted\n   219\t   (escaping backslash and quote, the only two escapes there), ints bare.\n   220\t   Key coercion (numeric strings to ints) is left to PHP itself, exactly as\n   221\t   the engine's `php/array-key` performs it.\"\n   222\t  [v]\n   223\t  (cond (string? v) (str \"'\" (str/replace v #\"\\\\|'\" (fn [[c]] (str \"\\\\\" c))) \"'\")\n   224\t        (integer? v) (str v)\n   225\t        :else (throw (ex-info \"p5 oracle: non-scalar in request record\" {:value v}))))\n   226\t\n   227\t(defn- request-pairs\n   228\t  \"Ordered `[k v]` pairs of request-array `arr`, following its `:order`\n   229\t   (the engine's insertion order).\"\n   230\t  [arr]\n   231\t  (when arr\n   232\t    (mapv (fn [k] [k (get (:index arr) k)]) (:order arr))))\n   233\t\n   234\t(defn- php-array-literal\n   235\t  \"The PHP `array(...)` literal of request-array `arr`.\"\n   236\t  [arr]\n   237\t  (if (empty? (request-pairs arr))\n   238\t    \"array()\"\n   239\t    (str \"array(\"\n   240\t         (str/join \", \" (map (fn [[k v]]\n   241\t                               (str (php-literal k) \" => \" (php-literal v)))\n   242\t                             (request-pairs arr)))\n   243\t         \")\")))\n   244\t\n   245\t(defn p5-prologue\n   246\t  \"The `auto_prepend_file` prologue assigning the superglobals from the\n   247\t   fixture `:request` record, mirroring `php/bind-request!` (prelude\n   248\t   section `request and output`): `$_GET` is the query, `$_POST` the body,\n   249\t   `$_COOKIE` the cookies, `$_SERVER` the server fields with\n   250\t   `REQUEST_METHOD`/`REQUEST_URI` appended, `$_ENV` the env, `$_FILES` the\n   251\t   files, and `$_REQUEST` is `array_merge($_GET, $_POST)` (POST wins, the\n   252\t   engine's `php/merge-loop` over `[get post]`).\"\n   253\t  [request]\n   254\t  (let [method (or (:php.request/method request) \"\")\n   255\t        uri (or (:php.request/uri request) \"\")]\n   256\t    (str \"<?php\\n\"\n   257\t         \"$_GET = \" (php-array-literal (:php.request/query request)) \";\\n\"\n   258\t         \"$_POST = \" (php-array-literal (:php.request/body request)) \";\\n\"\n   259\t         \"$_COOKIE = \" (php-array-literal (:php.request/cookies request)) \";\\n\"\n   260\t         \"$_SERVER = \" (php-array-literal (:php.request/server request)) \";\\n\"\n   261\t         \"$_SERVER['REQUEST_METHOD'] = \" (php-literal method) \";\\n\"\n   262\t         \"$_SERVER['REQUEST_URI'] = \" (php-literal uri) \";\\n\"\n   263\t         \"$_ENV = \" (php-array-literal (:php.request/env request)) \";\\n\"\n   264\t         \"$_FILES = \" (php-array-literal (:php.request/files request)) \";\\n\"\n   265\t         \"$_REQUEST = array_merge($_GET, $_POST);\\n\")))\n   266\t\n   267\t(defn run-php-file-with-prepend\n   268\t  \"Run `<file>` inside `<dir>` via Docker `php:8.3-cli` with `prepend-file`\n   269\t   (a path relative to `<dir>`) as `auto_prepend_file`, and return the\n   270\t   parsed `{:out :diag :uncaught :exit}`.\"\n   271\t  [dir file prepend-file]\n   272\t  (let [{:keys [out err exit]}\n   273\t        (sh/sh \"docker\" \"run\" \"--rm\"\n   274\t               \"-v\" (str (.toAbsolutePath (.toPath (io/file dir))) \":/w\")\n   275\t               \"-w\" \"/w\"\n   276\t               \"php:8.3-cli\" \"php\"\n   277\t               \"-d\" \"display_errors=1\"\n   278\t               \"-d\" \"html_errors=0\"\n   279\t               \"-d\" \"error_reporting=E_ALL\"\n   280\t               \"-d\" \"log_errors=0\"\n   281\t               \"-d\" (str \"auto_prepend_file=/w/\" prepend-file)\n   282\t               file\n   283\t               :out-enc \"UTF-8\")]\n   284\t    (assoc (parse-stdout out file nil)\n   285\t           :err err\n   286\t           :exit exit)))\n   287\t\n   288\t(defn check-p5-fixture\n   289\t  \"Run P5 `fixture` in temporary directory `dir`: the fixture source plus,\n   290\t   for `:request`-bearing fixtures, the [[p5-prologue]] as\n   291\t   `auto_prepend_file`. Returns a check record like [[check-fixture]].\"\n   292\t  [dir {:keys [id source request out diag uncaught oracle], :as fixture}]\n   293\t  (let [file (str (name id) \".php\")\n   294\t        pre (str (name id) \"-pre.php\")]\n   295\t    (write-source! dir file source)\n   296\t    (when request (write-source! dir pre (p5-prologue request)))\n   297\t    (let [actual (if request\n   298\t                   (run-php-file-with-prepend dir file pre)\n   299\t                   (run-php-file dir file))\n   300\t          expected-out (or out \"\")\n   301\t          expected-diag (vec (or diag []))\n   302\t          pass? (and (not= :pending oracle)\n   303\t                     (= expected-out (:out actual))\n   304\t                     (= expected-diag (:diag actual))\n   305\t                     (= uncaught (:uncaught actual)))]\n   306\t      {:id id,\n   307\t       :pass? pass?,\n   308\t       :oracle oracle,\n   309\t       :expected {:out expected-out, :diag expected-diag, :uncaught uncaught},\n   310\t       :actual (select-keys actual [:out :diag :uncaught])})))\n   311\t\n   312\t(defn run-p5\n   313\t  \"Run all `p5/fixtures` (the request-context fixtures) against\n   314\t   `php:8.3-cli`.\"\n   315\t  []\n   316\t  (let [dir (.toFile (Files/createTempDirectory \"yang-php-oracle-p5-\"\n   317\t                                                (make-array FileAttribute 0)))]\n   318\t    (try\n   319\t      (mapv #(check-p5-fixture dir %) p5/fixtures)\n   320\t      (finally\n   321\t        (doseq [f (reverse (file-seq dir))]\n   322\t          (.delete ^java.io.File f))))))\n   323\t\n   324\t(defn print-fold\n   325\t  \"Print the fold lines for `results`: one paste-ready record per fixture\n   326\t   in the P4 [[p4/pin]] shape `{:oracle banner :out :diag :uncaught}`.\"\n   327\t  [results]\n   328\t  (doseq [{:keys [id actual]} results]\n   329\t    (println \"FOLD\" (name id)\n   330\t             (pr-str (assoc (select-keys actual [:out :diag :uncaught])\n   331\t                            :oracle banner)))))\n   332\t\n   333\t(defn run-all\n   334\t  \"Run all `programs/fixtures`, `matrix-source` and `float-cases` against\n   335\t   `php:8.3-cli`.\"\n   336\t  []\n   337\t  (let [dir (.toFile (Files/createTempDirectory \"yang-php-oracle-\"\n   338\t                                                (make-array FileAttribute 0)))]\n   339\t    (try\n   340\t      (-> (mapv #(check-fixture dir %) (concat programs/fixtures p3b/all-fixtures p4/all-fixtures p6/all-fixtures))\n   341\t          (conj (check-matrix dir))\n   342\t          (conj (check-floats dir)))\n   343\t      (finally\n   344\t        (doseq [f (reverse (file-seq dir))]\n   345\t          (.delete ^java.io.File f))))))\n   346\t\n   347\t\n   348\t(defn -main\n   349\t  [& args]\n   350\t  (when (some #{\"--print-prologue\"} args)\n   351\t    (let [id (keyword (or (second (drop-while #(not= \"--print-prologue\" %) args))\n   352\t                          \"superglobals-from-request\"))\n   353\t          fixture (first (filter #(= id (:id %)) p5/fixtures))]\n   354\t      (when-not fixture\n   355\t        (println \"Unknown P5 fixture:\" id)\n   356\t        (System/exit 2))\n   357\t      ;; Dry run: no docker, no oracle. Print the generated prologue for\n   358\t      ;; eyeball comparison against the engine's expected superglobal\n   359\t      ;; values (the fixture's hand-derived :out is the reference).\n   360\t      (print (p5-prologue (:request fixture)))\n   361\t      (flush)\n   362\t      (shutdown-agents)\n   363\t      (System/exit 0)))\n   364\t  (when (some #{\"--p5\"} args)\n   365\t    (let [results (run-p5)\n   366\t          recorded (filter #(= :pending (:oracle %)) results)\n   367\t          failures (remove #(or (:pass? %) (= :pending (:oracle %))) results)]\n   368\t      (println \"Banner:\" banner)\n   369\t      (println \"Checked:\" (count results) \"P5 targets; failures:\" (count failures))\n   370\t      (print-fold recorded)\n   371\t      (doseq [f failures]\n   372\t        (println \"FAIL\" (:id f))\n   373\t        (println \"  expected:\" (pr-str (:expected f)))\n   374\t        (println \"  actual:  \" (pr-str (:actual f))))\n   375\t      (shutdown-agents)\n   376\t      (when (seq failures)\n   377\t        (System/exit 1))\n   378\t      (System/exit 0)))\n   379\t  (let [results (run-all)\n   380\t        recorded (filter #(= :pending (:oracle %)) results)\n   381\t        failures (remove #(or (:pass? %) (= :pending (:oracle %))) results)]\n   382\t    (println \"Banner:\" banner)\n   383\t    (println \"Checked:\" (count results) \"targets; failures:\" (count failures))\n   384\t    (doseq [f recorded]\n   385\t      (println \"RECORD\" (:id f) (pr-str (:actual f)) \"matches-pinned-out:\" (boolean (:pass? f))))\n   386\t    (doseq [f failures]\n   387\t      (println \"FAIL\" (:id f))\n   388\t      (println \"  expected:\" (pr-str (:expected f)))\n   389\t      (println \"  actual:  \" (pr-str (:actual f))))\n   390\t    (shutdown-agents)\n   391\t    (when (seq failures)\n   392\t      (System/exit 1))))\n     1\t(ns yang.php.antlr.programs-p5\n     2\t  \"P5 request-context fixtures. Expectations are hand-derived from PHP 8.3;\n     3\t  every fixture remains available to the oracle recording pass.\")\n     4\t\n     5\t\n     6\t(defn request-array\n     7\t  [entries]\n     8\t  {:php/type :array, :index (into {} entries), :order (mapv first entries)})\n     9\t\n    10\t\n    11\t(def request\n    12\t  {:php.request/method \"POST\"\n    13\t   :php.request/uri \"/hello?a=1\"\n    14\t   :php.request/query (request-array [[\"a\" \"1\"] [\"shared\" \"get\"]])\n    15\t   :php.request/headers (request-array [[\"X-Test\" \"yes\"]])\n    16\t   :php.request/cookies (request-array [[\"session\" \"abc\"]])\n    17\t   :php.request/body (request-array [[\"b\" \"2\"] [\"shared\" \"post\"]])\n    18\t   :php.request/server (request-array [[\"SERVER_NAME\" \"fixture.test\"]])\n    19\t   :php.request/env (request-array [[\"APP_ENV\" \"test\"]])\n    20\t   :php.request/files (request-array [[\"upload\" \"fixture\"]])})\n    21\t\n    22\t\n    23\t(defn- fx\n    24\t  [id source out & {:as more}]\n    25\t  (merge {:id id, :group :request-context, :source source, :out out,\n    26\t          :request request, :oracle :pending}\n    27\t         more))\n    28\t\n    29\t\n    30\t(def fixtures\n    31\t  [(fx :superglobals-from-request\n    32\t       (str \"<?php echo $_GET['a'], $_POST['b'], $_COOKIE['session'],\"\n    33\t            \" $_SERVER['REQUEST_METHOD'], $_SERVER['REQUEST_URI'],\"\n    34\t            \" $_SERVER['SERVER_NAME'], $_ENV['APP_ENV'], $_FILES['upload'],\"\n    35\t            \" $_REQUEST['a'], $_REQUEST['b'], $_REQUEST['shared'];\")\n    36\t       \"12abcPOST/hello?a=1fixture.testtestfixture12post\" :diag [] :oracle \"php-8.3.35 shiva 2026-10-25\")\n    37\t   (fx :output-buffering\n    38\t       \"<?php ob_start(); echo 'a'; echo ob_get_contents(); ob_start(); echo 'b'; echo ob_get_clean(); echo ob_get_clean(); echo 'c';\"\n    39\t       \"aabc\" :diag [] :oracle \"php-8.3.35 shiva 2026-10-25\")\n    40\t   (fx :output-buffer-flush\n    41\t       \"<?php ob_start(); echo 'a'; ob_end_flush(); echo 'b'; var_dump(ob_end_clean());\"\n    42\t       \"abbool(false)\\n\" :diag [[8 \"ob_end_clean(): Failed to delete buffer. No buffer to delete\"]] :oracle \"php-8.3.35 shiva 2026-10-25\")\n    43\t   (fx :headers-cookies-status\n    44\t       \"<?php header('X-One: 1'); setcookie('sid', 'abc'); http_response_code(201); echo http_response_code();\"\n    45\t       \"201\" :diag [] :oracle \"php-8.3.35 shiva 2026-10-25\"\n    46\t       :response [{:php.response/header \"X-One: 1\", :replace true}\n    47\t                  {:php.response/cookie {:name \"sid\", :value \"abc\"}}\n    48\t                  {:php.response/status 201}\n    49\t                  {:php.response/body \"201\"}])\n    50\t   (fx :headers-after-output\n    51\t       \"<?php echo 'x'; header('X-Late: 1'); var_dump(headers_sent());\"\n    52\t       \"xbool(true)\\n\" :diag [[2 \"Cannot modify header information - headers already sent by (output started at /w/headers-after-output.php:1)\"]] :oracle \"php-8.3.35 shiva 2026-10-25\"\n    53\t       :response [{:php.response/body \"xbool(true)\\n\"}])\n    54\t   (fx :error-handler-and-warnings\n    55\t       (str \"<?php set_error_handler(function($n, $s) { echo 'H', $n, ':', $s; });\"\n    56\t            \" trigger_error('first', E_USER_WARNING); restore_error_handler();\"\n    57\t            \" trigger_error('second', E_USER_NOTICE);\")\n    58\t       \"H512:first\" :diag [[8 \"second\"]] :oracle \"php-8.3.35 shiva 2026-10-25\")\n    59\t   (fx :exit-runs-shutdown\n    60\t       \"<?php register_shutdown_function(function() { echo 'S'; }); echo 'A'; exit(7); echo 'B';\"\n    61\t       \"AS\" :diag [] :oracle \"php-8.3.35 shiva 2026-10-25\"\n    62\t       :status 7)\n    63\t   (fx :exit-string\n    64\t       \"<?php echo 'A'; die('B'); echo 'C';\"\n    65\t       \"AB\" :diag [] :oracle \"php-8.3.35 shiva 2026-10-25\"\n    66\t       :status 0)])\n6:    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p5 :as p5]))\n11:  (mapv (juxt :errno :message) (:php/diag r)))\n19:  (doseq [{:keys [id source request out diag response status]} p5/fixtures]\n32:        request-a (assoc p5/request :php.request/query (p5/request-array [[\"value\" \"A\"]]))\n33:        request-b (assoc p5/request :php.request/query (p5/request-array [[\"value\" \"B\"]]))\n# P5 request context findings\n\n## Delivered\n\n- Bound `$_GET`, `$_POST`, `$_COOKIE`, `$_SERVER`, `$_ENV`, `$_FILES`, and `$_REQUEST` from an explicit, task-local request record. Request collections accept either PHP arrays or ordered entry vectors; missing collections become empty arrays. `$_REQUEST` uses GET-then-POST replacement order.\n- Added output-buffer stack operations, ordered response records for headers/cookies/status/body, and headers-after-output diagnostics.\n- Lowered both `exit`/`die` parser forms to the runtime exit path. Exit runs shutdown functions, returns its status, and is not reported as an uncaught error.\n- Added user error triggering, handler restoration, `getenv`, and `php_sapi_name` registrations.\n- Added eight hand-derived P5 fixtures, all marked `:oracle :pending`, plus an independent-task isolation test using two separate VM sessions.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `clojure -M:test -n yang.php.antlr.request-context-test`: 3 tests, 35 assertions, all passing.\n- `clojure -M:test -n yang.php.antlr.class-model-test -n yang.php.antlr.objects-test -n yang.php.antlr.generators-test`: 14 tests, 1201 assertions, all passing.\n- `clojure -M:kondo --lint` over all changed Clojure files: 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n- Managed `cljstyle 0.17.642` check over all changed Clojure files: passing.\n- `git diff --check`: passing.\n\nNo PHP oracle recording was performed, as requested for this round. No push was performed.\n# SEAT-RUN instructions: P5 oracle recording on shiva\n\n## What landed (uncommitted on `feat/p5-oracle-recording`)\n\n`src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj` extended for programs-P5:\n\n- `p5-prologue` builds the `auto_prepend_file` prologue assigning\n  `$_GET`/`$_POST`/`$_COOKIE`/`$_SERVER`/`$_ENV`/`$_FILES`/`$_REQUEST`\n  from the fixture `:request` record, mirroring `php/bind-request!`\n  (`src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc`, section `request and output`):\n  `$_GET` = query, `$_POST` = body, `$_COOKIE` = cookies,\n  `$_SERVER` = server fields with `REQUEST_METHOD`/`REQUEST_URI`\n  appended, `$_ENV` = env, `$_FILES` = files,\n  `$_REQUEST = array_merge($_GET, $_POST)` (POST wins).\n- `run-php-file-with-prepend`, `check-p5-fixture`, `run-p5`,\n  `print-fold` (P4 `pin` shape per fixture).\n- `-main` modes: `--p5` (run only P5 fixtures), `--print-prologue [id]`\n  (dry run, no docker).\n\nVerified here (no docker): `--print-prologue` output for\n`:superglobals-from-request` hand-checked against the engine's expected\nsuperglobal values — concatenating the prologue's values in the\nfixture source's echo order yields exactly the fixture `:out`\n(`12abcPOST/hello?a=1fixture.testtesttestfixture12post`).\n`clojure -M:test -n yang.php.antlr.request-context-test` green\n(3 tests, 35 assertions). kondo/cljstyle binaries absent on this\nmachine — run them on shiva before folding.\n\nNOTE: `p5/fixtures` holds **8** request-context fixtures, not 9\n(superglobals-from-request, output-buffering, output-buffer-flush,\nheaders-cookies-status, headers-after-output, error-handler-and-warnings,\nexit-runs-shutdown, exit-string). If the seat expects a 9th, say which.\n\n## Run on shiva\n\n```sh\ncd /path/to/datomworld-p5r   # feat/p5-oracle-recording\ngit pull                      # after this commit is pushed, or copy the tree\ntimeout 300 clojure -M:dev:test -m yang.php.oracle --p5\n```\n\nUses `docker run --rm php:8.3-cli` per fixture (same flags as the\nexisting runner, plus `-d auto_prepend_file=/w/<id>-pre.php`).\nNeeds docker + `php:8.3-cli`; `timeout 300` covers the whole pass\n(each `docker run` inherits no per-run timeout — same as existing\nrunner; add `timeout 300 docker ...` per run if shiva is slow).\n\n## What to paste back for the fold\n\nThe full stdout, in particular every `FOLD <id> {...}` line:\n\n```\nFOLD <id> {:out \"...\" :diag [...] :uncaught ... :oracle \"<banner>\"}\n```\n\nFold rule (P4 `pin` shape): recorded values override hand-authored\npins; on the implementor side, paste each `FOLD` map into the\n`recorded` map keyed by id and re-run\n`yang.php.antlr.request-context-test`. A fixture whose recorded\n`:out`/`:diag`/`:uncaught` differs from the hand-derived pin is a\nreal discrepancy — report it, do not silently keep the pin.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
