e or a reason,\\\" `rpc.cljc:128-134`; every `request!` outcome covered with `invalid-request` unreachable because the materializer always supplies keyword op + vector args) is accurate.\\ncollab/dao-jing/1788959908204-storage-space-index-phase3.glm-5.3.findings.md:56:returned, so P5's ownership rule holds structurally on this path too.\\ncollab/dao-jing/1788959908204-storage-space-index-phase3.glm-5.3.findings.md:75:| P5 | failed open closes its store | **new** query_test `failed-open-closes-the-store-it-opened`: a close-counting store whose `:get-content-fn` throws after `jing-coordinate/open!` succeeds; asserts the *identical* error object propagates and the store closed **exactly once** (cljd branch skips — with-redefs) |\\ncollab/dao-jing/1788959908204-storage-space-index-phase3.glm-5.3.findings.md:165:- cljd skips the with-redefs harnesses (#5-moved, P5) with an `is true`\\ncollab/dao-jing/1788959908204-storage-space-index-phase3.prompt.md:59:**Plus P5, a test the adapter never had:** \\\"a store opened during a failed\\ncollab/yang-python/1792197000000-architect-yang-ts-php-designs.claude-cloud-fable.findings.md:268:**Scope**: PHP has function scope only, no block scope, no implicit closure capture (except arrow `fn`, which captures by value every enclosing variable it mentions, at creation). Locals are cells allocated at function entry with `:php/undef` (a read emits `Warning: Undefined variable` and yields null). `global $x` binds the local cell to a marker on the `$GLOBALS` entry (creating it as null if absent). `static $x = init;` is a cell owned by the function object, allocated once at function definition (constant expression initializer evaluated once). **Dynamic scope profile**: a function body that contains `include`/`require`, `$$name`, `extract`, `compact`, `get_defined_vars`, `eval` or `parse_str` with one argument has its locals in a heap symbol-table dict (the Python module-namespace precedent, owner decision 1 of 8.5.1); scope analysis decides per function, and the lowering targets `php/local-get`/`php/local-set` on the dict. All other functions use cells. The global scope is always the `$GLOBALS` dict (a heap dict, insertion-ordered, with the superglobals pre-seeded by the request record). `$GLOBALS` itself is read-only as of PHP 8.1 except through its elements, which fits.\\ncollab/yang-python/1792197000000-architect-yang-ts-php-designs.claude-cloud-fable.findings.md:270:**Superglobals and the request context** (ADR 0004 doctrine; §8.6): a PHP run is one task consuming one **request record** from a composition-supplied stream (`{:php.request/method :uri :query :headers :cookies :body :server :env :files}`), from which `php/init!` builds `$_GET`, `$_POST`, `$_COOKIE`, `$_SERVER`, `$_ENV`, `$_FILES`, `$_REQUEST` (ordered per `request_order` pin) and `$argv`/`$argc` for CLI; `$_SESSION` is a bound surface (session store effect), absent by default. Nothing reads ambient process or HTTP state. Output (`echo`, `print`, inline HTML, `printf`) appends to an output cell with the output-buffering stack (`ob_start`/`ob_get_clean` are pure prelude over that stack); the top level flushes as ordered `:php.response/body` records on the response stream; `header()`, `http_response_code`, `setcookie` are `:php.response/header` records (refused after the first body flush with the PHP warning text). `exit`/`die` is an escape to the task root, then flush. Cross-request state leakage is impossible by construction: one task per request and no store writes for guest state (Phase 3 exit criterion).\\ncollab/yang-python/1792197000000-architect-yang-ts-php-designs.claude-cloud-fable.findings.md:320:**Prelude inventory**, module `php` (reserved), hook prelude `phpsp`; `php/init!` builds the class table with the builtin classes and interfaces (`stdClass`, `Closure`, `Generator`, `ArrayObject` deferred, `Traversable`, `Iterator`, `IteratorAggregate`, `ArrayAccess`, `Countable`, `Stringable`, `JsonSerializable`, `UnitEnum`/`BackedEnum`, the `Throwable` hierarchy), the function table with the supported builtins, `$GLOBALS` from the request record, the output-buffer stack, the error-handler cell, the included-files dict, and flips `php.rt/state` to `:php/ready`.\\ncollab/yang-python/1792197000000-architect-yang-ts-php-designs.claude-cloud-fable.findings.md:362:|                            | request is one task reading one request record   |            |\\ncollab/yang-python/1792197000000-architect-yang-ts-php-designs.claude-cloud-fable.findings.md:398:| P5 | Request context: `$_*` from the request record, `ob_*`, headers/cookies/status as response records, `exit`, error handler, warnings stream | superglobals reproducible from a fixture record (exit criterion 3); headers-after-output warning; two requests in two tasks share nothing (exit criterion 5) |\\ncollab/yang-python/1792197000000-architect-yang-ts-php-designs.claude-cloud-fable.findings.md:433:|                      | traits, many small included units, a request record fixture per  |\\ncollab/yang-python/1792197000000-architect-yang-ts-php-designs.claude-cloud-fable.findings.md:437:|                      | exit criteria 1-5 are direct fixtures (P1, P2/P3, P5, P4, P5)     |\\ncollab/yin-repl/1790442434240-architect-serve-decisions.claude-fable-5-1.prompt.md:6:# Task: decide dao.stream.serve section 15 under the owner invariant\\ncollab/yin-repl/1790442434240-architect-serve-decisions.claude-fable-5-1.prompt.md:31:Read in full: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.serve.md (section 15\\ncollab/yin-repl/1790442434240-architect-serve-decisions.claude-fable-5-1.prompt.md:57:3. THE EIGHT DECISIONS. For each of the eight items in section 15, in order: DECISION\\ncollab/dao-jing/1788977648939-architect-jing-remote-v2-plan.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:340:`jing-coordinate/open!` failing before a store is retained (its P5 cleanup\\ncollab/jolt/1793079899150-architect-j4d-review.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:221:- P5 Cross-host reope