st on every lane, slow ones included (JVM takes 20+ min)\\\\nbb test:slow         # Only the slow tests, on every lane\\\\n# One lane alone: <task>:clj, <task>:cljs, <task>:cljd\\\\nbb test:clj          # JVM, fast: skips ^:slow (bare `clj -M:test` runs them too)\\\\nbb test:cljs         # Node (shadow-cljs :cljs alias), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\\\\nbb test:cljd         # Dart (needs flutter on PATH), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\\\\nbb test:all:clj      # JVM, no filter: `clojure -M:test`\\\\nbb test:all:cljs     # Node with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\\\\nbb test:all:cljd     # Dart with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\\\\nbb test:slow:clj     # JVM: `-i :slow` (long-loops-test, ~14 min)\\\\nbb test:slow:cljs    # Node: only the namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\\\\nbb test:slow:cljd    # Dart: only those namespaces' generated tests, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\\\\n# Slow tests: tag a deftest ^:slow. The JVM runner then excludes it from `bb test:clj`.\\\\n# Node and Dart have no tag filter, so a .cljc slow test also wraps its body in\\\\n# (dao.test-slow/guard \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\" (fn [] ...)); it prints SKIP unless DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1.\\\\n# Node and Dart select slow tests by NAMESPACE (derived by grepping `slow/guard`\\\\n# under test/), so the non-slow tests inside those namespaces also run there.\\\\n# On Node, shadow also runs the test namespaces those nine require (about\\\\n# seven more, e.g. lower-portable-test); on Dart only the nine namespaces run.\\\\n# Run test:slow / test:all before a big merge or a commit that touches many parts.\\\\n# Run one Dart lane at a time per machine (the limit is cores and the Flutter cache,\\\\n# not subsystems). On the many-core remote hosts see \\\\\\\"Remote test servers\\\\\\\" below for\\\\n# which lanes may overlap.\\\\n#\\\\n# When to tag a test slow: when it takes more than about 5 s on any lane (the\\\\n# Python e2e tests sit on a ~3 s floor, so their JVM cut is 3.0 s). The\\\\n# default lanes must stay in minutes; 22 JVM tests (0.75% of the suite) were\\\\n# 81% of its test time. Tag it ^:slow on the JVM; if it is a .cljc test, also\\\\n# wrap its body in dao.test-slow/guard so Node and Dart skip it by default. A\\\\n# test that is slow only on Dart (dao.jing.dht-test/unproven-chunks-... takes\\\\n# 72 s there, 3.6 s on the JVM) is a candidate for a speed investigation first.\\\\n# Python slow set (2026-10-06): 65 ^:slow and 15 guard-only tests in the\\\\n# yang.python.antlr e2e, e2e-c1, prelude-parity, safepoint, float-address\\\\n# and int-contract tests; a Python slice landing runs `bb test:sub:clj yang.python --slow`\\\\n# (or `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n <ns>`).\\\\n# While iterating, use the Gate Ladder (see below): G0 iterate via `bb test:sub:clj <own>`\\\\n# or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`. Do not run the full `bb test` while iterating.\\\\n# At slice checkpoints, run G1 (`bb test:sub <own>`). Before landing a slice, run\\\\n# G2 (`bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes).\\\\n# Full repo-wide `bb test` (G3) is the mandatory landing gate on master after merge.\\\\n# Cross-host bugs show only on Node or Dar\\n\\n[elided: chars [4096, 1978730)]\\n\\n[preview: chars [1978730, 1979754)]\\nd_output\\\":\\\"mise ERROR error parsing config file: ~/workspace/datomworld-yang-h2/mise.toml\\\\nmise ERROR Config files in ~/workspace/datomworld-yang-h2/mise.toml are not trusted.\\\\nTrust them with `mise trust`. See https://mise.jdx.dev/cli/trust.html for more information.\\\\nmise ERROR Run with --verbose or MISE_VERBOSE=1 for more information\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":1,\\\"status\\\":\\\"failed\\\"}}\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793299000000-engineer-hardening2-fixround.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:69:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_36\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"rg --files /Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/cljstyle /Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs 2>/dev/null | rg '/cljstyle\\\\\\\"'$'\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\nResults truncated to 100 lines (total: 539 of a partial result set). Use offset=100 to see more.\\n[Output truncated at 10485760 bytes of rg output — the result set is incomplete. Narrow the pattern, path, or glob filters and re-run to recover complete results.]\"}\n{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"type\":\"function\",\"id\":\"tool_LzRfKAh52jSPdZ01Z058Gf2E\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"Read\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"path\\\":\\\"docs/agents/format.md\\\"}\"}}]}\n{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"tool_LzRfKAh52jSPdZ01Z058Gf2E\",\"content\":\"1\\t---\\n2\\tdescription: File and content format rules for datom.world — .chp/.blog EDN+Hiccup files, tables in .md files, and git commit message format\\n3\\t---\\n4\\t\\n5\\t# FORMATS\\n6\\t\\n7\\t`.chp` and `.blog` files are EDN files with Hiccup markup.\\n8\\t\\n9\\t## Structure for .blog files\\n10\\t\\n11\\t```clojure\\n12\\t#:blog{:title \\\"Title Here\\\"\\n13\\t       :date #inst \\\"YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.000-00:00\\\"\\n14\\t       :abstract [:p \\\"Abstract with hiccup markup...\\\"]\\n15\\t       :content [:section.blog-article\\n16\\t                 [:div.section-inner\\n17\\t                  [:article\\n18\\t                   :$blog-title\\n19\\t                   :$blog-date\\n20\\t                   ;; Hiccup content here\\n21\\t                   ]]]}\\n22\\t```\\n23\\t\\n24\\t## Guidelines for .blog files\\n25\\t\\n26\\t- Use EDN syntax with namespaced maps (`#:blog{...}`)\\n27\\t- Use Hiccup vectors for all markup (`[:p \\\"text\\\"]`, `[:strong \\\"bold\\\"]`, `[:a {:href \\\"...\\\"} \\\"link\\\"]`)\\n28\\t- Never use markdown syntax\\n29\\t- Include `:$blog-title` and `:$blog-date` where appropriate\\n30\\t- Never use em dashes (—). Use commas, colons, periods, or parentheses instead.\\n31\\t\\n32\\t## Tables in .md files\\n33\\t\\n34\\tTables in `.md` files (design documents, agent guides) are ASCII box tables,\\n35\\tnever markdown pipe tables:\\n36\\t\\n37\\t+-------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+\\n38\\t| Rule              | Detail                                                                    |\\n39\\t+===================+===========================================================================+\\n40\\t| Borders           | `+`, `-`, and `|` draw the box; a `+===+` rule separates the header row   |\\n41\\t|                   | from the body; every row closes with a full `+---+` border                |\\n42\\t+-------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+\\n43\\t| Maximum width     | 170 columns, counted in characters (UTF-8 aware), including the borders   |\\n44\\t+-------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+\\n45\\t| Column widths     | Columns that fit at their natural width stay unwrapped; wide columns      |\\n46\\t|                   | share the remaining budget proportionally to their content                |\\n47\\t+-------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+\\n48\\t| Wrapping          | Long cell content word-wraps onto continuation lines that carry only the  |\\n49\\t|                   | wrapped column; other columns are blank on continuation lines; an         |\\n50\\t|                   | unbreakable token longer than its column hard-breaks at the column edge   |\\n51\\t+-------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+\\n52\\t\\n53\\tThe example table above is itself in the format: `docs/agents/team.md` and\\n54\\t`docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md` are the reference\\n55\\tinstances (the previous second instance, the v3 `yin.vm.semantic.md`, was\\n56\\tdeleted at the 2026-10-15 cutover and its replacement carries no border\\n57\\ttables).\\n58\\t\\n59\\t## Git commit messages\\n60\\t\\n61\\tThis is a repository-wide convention, not specific to any one role. Commit\\n62\\tsubjects use:\\n63\\t\\n64\\t```text\\n65\\t<type>[(<scope>)]: <lowercase imperative summary>\\n66\\t```\\n67\\t\\n68\\t`type` is one of `docs|feat|fix|refactor|perf|test|build|chore`. An optional\\n69\\tbody explains non-obvious behavior or invariants; omit it when the subject\\n70\\tline is self-explanatory. Use no trailing period on the subject line. Merge\\n71\\tcommits are exempt from this format. Never add `Co-Authored-By`, including\\n72\\tLLM attribution, to any commit in this repository.\\n73\\t\\n74\\tWhether and when a commit is *allowed* to happen (review requirements,\\n75\\tauthorization, undoing an unauthorized commit) is role-specific policy, not\\n76\\tformat — see [`roles/orchestrator.md`](roles/orchestrator.md)'s Coordination\\n77\\tcontract for the orchestrator's own gating rules.\"}\n{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"The required PHP regressions pass: 14 tests, 1201 assertions. I’m checking the repository’s exact lint/format commands and reviewing the final diff for scope.\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"type\":\"function\",\"id\":\"tool_oMsWMWtmyW6unVdXD5D83CbR\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"Grep\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"path\\\":\\\"docs/agents/build-n-test.md\\\",\\\"pattern\\\":\\\"cljstyle|clj-kondo\\\",\\\"output_mode\\\":\\\"content\\\",\\\"-C\\\":4,\\\"head_limit\\\":100}\"}}]}\n{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"tool_oMsWMWtmyW6unVdXD5D83CbR\",\"content\":\"docs/agents/build-n-test.md-88-needed builds. `test:changed:list` shows what and why; `:clj`/`:cljs`/\\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md-89-`:cljd` run one lane; `--base REF`; `--changed FILE...` (absolute OK; a\\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md-90-typo, an empty list or the wrong cwd exits 1). Use it to iterate and to\\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md-91-land a slice confined to a package. Exit 2 (from :list too) is a wide\\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.m