) lands on branch `yang-php-p3b`; the oracle is the pinned `php-8.3.35`\\n--\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-57-Request records, bound surfaces and the refusal of ambient resolution follow\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-58-the doctrine of ADR 0004 (\\\"external effects are interpreted stream deposits\\\"),\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-59-which is Proposed and not yet committed; `yang.typescript.md` section 2.4\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-60-names what its rejection would reopen.\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-61-\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-62-## 1. Scope\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-63-\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-64-A new ANTLR frontend replaces the current PHP compiler frontend (section 5).\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-65-It compiles PHP 8.3 source, including\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-66-mixed HTML text, to the Universal AST, and runs one request as one task\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:67:reading an explicit request record. The frontend id is `:yang/php` either\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-68-way — the one-frontend-per-language scheme (2026-10-18; the id was\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-69-`:yang.php/legacy` before the legacy suffix was retired) leaves no room\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-70-for implementation-suffixed ids, so the ANTLR frontend lands as a new\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-71-revision of `:yang/php`, its implementation named by the manifest's\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-72-revision and profile keys; the final naming at acceptance is the owner's.\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-73-\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-74-The design claims a specified fragment, not Zend fidelity: the transition\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-75-table of section 4 and the behaviour of the slices of section 15, each pinned\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-76-by oracle fixtures against the pinned PHP CLI, with every Zend behaviour\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-77-outside it listed as a named corner (section 17). The `yang.antlr.md` Phase 3\\n--\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-192-  declaration** (PHP 8.3) and filled once.\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-193-- **The dynamic-scope profile**: a function whose body contains\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-194-  `include`/`require`, `$$name`, `extract`, `compact`, `get_defined_vars`,\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-195-  `eval`, or one-argument `parse_str` keeps its locals in a heap symbol-table\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-196-  dict (the precedent is Python's module namespace, owner decision 1 of\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-197-  `yang.antlr.md` 8.5.1). Scope analysis decides per function, and the\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-198-  lowering targets `php/local-get`/`php/local-set` on the dict. All other\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-199-  functions use cells (owner decision B8.3). The symbol table holds reference\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-200-  markers like any location.\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-201-- **The global scope** is always the `$GLOBALS` dict: a heap dict,\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:202:  insertion-ordered, with the superglobals pre-seeded from the request record.\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-203-  `$GLOBALS` is read-only as of PHP 8.1 except through its elements (corner\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-204-  C13).\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-205-\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-206-### 3.4 Superglobals and the request context\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-207-\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:208:- A PHP run is one task consuming one **request record** from a\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-209-  composition-supplied stream: `{:php.request/method :uri :query :headers\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-210-  :cookies :body :server :env :files}`. `php/init!` builds `$_GET`, `$_POST`,\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-211-  `$_COOKIE`, `$_SERVER`, `$_ENV`, `$_FILES`, `$_REQUEST` (ordered per a\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-212-  pinned `request_order`) and, for CLI, `$argv` and `$argc`. `$_SESSION` is a\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-213-  bound surface (a session-store effect), absent by default. Nothing reads\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-214-  ambient process or HTTP state.\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md-215-- **Output** (`echo`, `print`, inline HTML, `pri