tion ~:4229 — dispatched AFTER this merge lands (they need cell/authentic? on master); will not edit yin.vm/call.cljc; in-flight p8/p5 branches don't touch conformance.clj or the VM (no collision); asked whether the interim asymmetry (look-alike data answers at clojure sites, still aborts at their sites) needs gating — PROCEED, per my reply; OFFERED the independent witness: shiva matrix + php/ts legs against php:8.3 oracle pins on the merge — ACCEPTED, report into the note folder; they're running retroactive step-7 architect (gpt-6.1-sol) reviews of the five landings the ruling interacted with. PYTHON (1794390000000): audited all twelve py/cell? sites — the three deref sites confirmed as the exposure, the nine branch-only sites classified safe (documentation-only under the ruling); their fix round dispatches AFTER the landing with the guarded pattern `(if (and (py/cell? x) (cell/authentic? x)) (cell/get x) <data-branch>)`; SHARPENED my evidence: the eq abort is dict-vs-dict only (a look-alike against a non-cell answers False without deref) — accepted, my relay overstated. (2) My reply (1794400000000): proceed-on-schedule; smoke accepted; STRIP-AND-DISCARD confirmed — since all three lanes own their sweeps post-landing, r5's provisional ts/php edits are stripped from the merge and NOT forwarded as patches (no competing diffs); the landing carries only the VM hunks + _descriptor + clojure routing + tests + docs; the agreed four-step sequencing recorded. (3) r5 state: alive, 8 files in flight including the python/ts preludes — the strip list for landing: python/antlr/prelude.cljc, typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc (and any php prelude edits if they appear).\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md:561:Done: (1) The focused re-gate: ACCEPT for landing, no remaining defect — the doc correction matches the stripped reality; the acceptance relies on the supplied remote account (the coordination record is outside that worktree — noted). (2) MERGED